@topic Not supported DOS features
@keys int86 intdos inportb outportb outp inp peek poke MK_FP FP_SEG FP_OFF getvect setvect gettext puttext movetext graphics initgraph farmalloc far near interrupt unsupported
 Not supported DOS features

 Flash C produces programs for 64-bit Linux, so features that depend
 on DOS, the PC BIOS or the hardware cannot be provided. Declarations
 for these are not in the headers, so a program that uses them gets an
 undefined-function error. Use the portable replacements where one
 exists.

 Not provided

   int86, int86x, intdos, intdosx, bdos, geninterrupt  (software interrupts)
   inportb, outportb, inport, outport, inp, outp        (I/O ports)
   peek, poke, peekb, pokeb, MK_FP, FP_SEG, FP_OFF      (far memory)
   getvect, setvect, keep, harderr, ctrlbrk              (interrupt handling)
   farmalloc, farfree, allocmem, coreleft                 (far heap)
   gettext, puttext, movetext                             (screen buffer)
   graphics.h: initgraph, line, circle and so on          (graphics)
   bioscom, biosdisk, bios_*, biosprint                   (BIOS devices)

 Replacements

   screen text      {cprintf}, {gotoxy}, {window}, {textcolor}
   keyboard         {getch}, {kbhit}, {bioskey}
   timing           {delay}, {sleep}, {time}, {clock}
   files            {Library: stdio}

 The keywords near, far, huge, cdecl and pascal are accepted and ignored.

 See {Differences from classic compilers}

@topic Predefined macros
@keys __FILE__ __LINE__ __DATE__ __TIME__ __STDC__
 Predefined macros

   __FILE__   the name of the source file as a string
   __LINE__   the current line number
   __DATE__   the compilation date, "Mmm dd yyyy"
   __TIME__   the compilation time, "hh:mm:ss"
   __STDC__   1

 See {Preprocessor}

@topic Preprocessor
@keys include define undef ifdef ifndef elif endif pragma line error defined
@alias Preprocessor directives
 Preprocessor

 Directives
   #include <file>   search the include directories
   #include "file"   search the current directory first
   #define NAME text / #define NAME(args) text
   #undef  NAME
   #if expr / #ifdef / #ifndef / #elif / #else / #endif
   #line number "file"
   #error text
   #pragma ...       startup and exit functions, others ignored

 Operators in macros: # makes a string, ## joins tokens.
 Defined in expressions: defined(NAME).

 See {Predefined macros}

