@topic div
@keys div
 div

 Divides two ints and returns quotient and remainder.

 Header: stdlib.h

 Syntax
   div_t div(int numer, int denom);

 The quotient is truncated toward zero. If the result cannot be
 represented the behavior is undefined.

 Return value
 A div_t with the members quot and rem.

 See also: {ldiv}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic div_t
@keys div_t
 div_t

 The structure returned by div: int quot (quotient) and int rem
 (remainder). ldiv_t is the same with long members.

 Back to {Library functions}

