 Nothing.

 See also: {delline}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic isalnum
@keys isalnum
 isalnum

 Tests whether a character is a letter or a digit.

 Header: ctype.h

 Syntax
   int isalnum(int c);

 The argument must be an unsigned char value or EOF. Same as
 isalpha(c) || isdigit(c).

 Return value
 Nonzero if the test is true, otherwise 0.

 See also: {tolower} {toupper}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic isalpha
@keys isalpha
 isalpha

 Tests whether a character is a letter.

 Header: ctype.h

 Syntax
   int isalpha(int c);

 The argument must be an unsigned char value or EOF. In the "C"
 locale: A-Z and a-z.

 Return value
 Nonzero if the test is true, otherwise 0.

 See also: {tolower} {toupper}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic iscntrl
@keys iscntrl
 iscntrl

 Tests whether a character is a control character.

 Header: ctype.h

 Syntax
   int iscntrl(int c);

 The argument must be an unsigned char value or EOF. In the "C"
 locale: codes 0 to 31 and 127.

 Return value
 Nonzero if the test is true, otherwise 0.

 See also: {tolower} {toupper}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic isdigit
@keys isdigit
 isdigit

 Tests whether a character is a decimal digit.

 Header: ctype.h

 Syntax
   int isdigit(int c);

 The argument must be an unsigned char value or EOF. The characters 0
 to 9.

 Return value
 Nonzero if the test is true, otherwise 0.

 See also: {tolower} {toupper}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic isgraph
@keys isgraph
 isgraph

 Tests whether a character is a printing character other than space.

 Header: ctype.h

 Syntax
   int isgraph(int c);

 The argument must be an unsigned char value or EOF. Codes 33 to 126.

 Return value
 Nonzero if the test is true, otherwise 0.

 See also: {tolower} {toupper}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic islower
@keys islower
 islower

 Tests whether a character is a lowercase letter.

 Header: ctype.h

 Syntax
   int islower(int c);

 The argument must be an unsigned char value or EOF. a-z in the "C"
 locale.

 Return value
 Nonzero if the test is true, otherwise 0.

 See also: {tolower} {toupper}

 Back to {Library functions}

