@topic kbhit
@keys kbhit
 kbhit

 Tests whether a key is waiting.

 Header: conio.h

 Syntax
   int kbhit(void);

 Does not read the key. Use getch to read it.

 Return value
 Nonzero if a key can be read, otherwise 0.

 See also: {getch}

 Back to {Library functions}

 Example

@example
#include <conio.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <dos.h>

int main(void)
{
    int n = 0;
    while (!kbhit()) {
        printf("\rwaiting %d", n++);
        fflush(stdout);
        delay(100);
    }
    getch();
    return 0;
}
@end

