@topic malloc
@keys malloc
 malloc

 Allocates memory.

 Header: stdlib.h

 Syntax
   void *malloc(size_t size);

 The block is not initialized. Free it with free. A request for size 0
 may return NULL or a unique pointer.

 Return value
 A pointer to the block (suitably aligned for any type), or NULL if
 there is not enough memory.

 See also: {calloc} {realloc} {free}

 Back to {Library functions}

 Example

@example
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

int main(void)
{
    char *s = malloc(32);
    if (s == NULL)
        return 1;
    strcpy(s, "dynamic");
    puts(s);
    free(s);
    return 0;
}
@end

