 Changes the system clock, which needs administrator privileges;
 without them the call has no effect.

 Return value
 Nothing.

 See also: {getdate} {settime}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic setjmp
@keys setjmp
 setjmp

 Saves the calling environment. (setjmp.h)

 Header: see description

 Syntax
   int setjmp(jmp_buf env);

 Returns 0 when called directly; when longjmp is used it returns the
 value given to longjmp.

 Return value
 0, or the value passed to longjmp.

 See also: {longjmp}

 Back to {Library functions}

 Example

@example
#include <setjmp.h>
#include <stdio.h>

static jmp_buf env;

static void fail(void)
{
    longjmp(env, 2);
}

int main(void)
{
    int r = setjmp(env);
    if (r == 0) {
        fail();
    } else {
        printf("recovered, code %d\n", r);
    }
    return 0;
}
@end

