@topic text_info
@keys text_info
 text_info

 struct text_info, filled by gettextinfo: unsigned char winleft,
 wintop, winright, winbottom (window corners), attribute (current
 colours), normattr (colours at start), currmode (text mode),
 screenheight, screenwidth, curx, cury (cursor position in the
 window). Declared in conio.h.

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic textattr
@keys textattr
 textattr

 Sets text colour and background together.

 Header: conio.h

 Syntax
   void textattr(int attr);

 attr = foreground + (background << 4), plus BLINK (128) for blinking.
 Colours are the constants listed in {Console colors}.

 Return value
 Nothing.

 See also: {textcolor} {textbackground}

 Back to {Library functions}

 Example

@example
#include <conio.h>

int main(void)
{
    textattr(YELLOW + (RED << 4));
    clrscr();
    cputs("Yellow on red");
    getch();
    normvideo();
    return 0;
}
@end

@topic textbackground
@keys textbackground
 textbackground

 Sets the background colour.

 Header: conio.h

 Syntax
   void textbackground(int color);

 color is 0 (BLACK) to 7 (LIGHTGRAY); see {Console colors}.

 Return value
 Nothing.

 See also: {textcolor} {textattr}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic textcolor
@keys textcolor
 textcolor

 Sets the foreground colour.

 Header: conio.h

 Syntax
   void textcolor(int color);

 color is 0 to 15, optionally plus BLINK; see {Console colors}.

 Return value
 Nothing.

 See also: {textbackground} {textattr}

 Back to {Library functions}

@topic textmode
@keys textmode
 textmode

 Selects a text mode.

 Header: conio.h

 Syntax
   void textmode(int mode);

 The terminal decides the real size. The call resets the window to the
 whole screen and the colours to normal. mode is one of BW40, C40,
 BW80, C80, MONO, C4350 or LASTMODE; only the screen size reported by
 gettextinfo follows the terminal, and the 43/50 line mode is not
 forced.

 Return value
 Nothing.

 See also: {gettextinfo} {window}

 Back to {Library functions}

