@topic ungetc
@keys ungetc
 ungetc

 Pushes a character back onto an input stream.

 Header: stdio.h

 Syntax
   int ungetc(int c, FILE *stream);

 One character of pushback is guaranteed. EOF cannot be pushed back. A
 successful fseek, fsetpos or rewind discards the pushed-back
 character.

 Return value
 c, or EOF on failure.

 See also: {fgetc} {fseek}

 Back to {Library functions}

